From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: load the T6050 combo PHYs before appledrm

appledrm already soft-depends on the display crossbar, because a DCP
probe that defers after the deferred probe timeout gives up its Type-C
routes for the boot. The routes' PHYs need the same: on T6050 they are
the combo PHYs of atc-t6050-dp, which appledrm does not otherwise pull
in.

On a J714s on macOS 27.3 (up273-8), appledrm probed from the root
filesystem at about 62 s, long after the 10 s timer, and dcpext0 and
dcpext2, the two engines with Type-C routes, failed with "deferred probe
timeout, ignoring dependency" and -110. dcpext1 and dcpext3 have no
routes and came up.

Candidate. Compiled on ush (the module info carries the new softdep);
not booted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
@@ -2120,7 +2120,9 @@
  * crossbar. Without this, initramfs generators leave it out, it loads only
  * from the root filesystem, and a DCP probe that waits past the deferred
  * probe timeout (an encrypted root's passphrase prompt) gives up its routes.
+ * The same holds for the PHYs of the routes: on T6050 they are the combo
+ * PHYs of atc-t6050-dp, which nothing else pulls in before this module.
  * DCP also asks for the battery temperature once while it starts (see
  * dcp_pmu_temperature()), so have the SMC battery registered by then.
  */
-MODULE_SOFTDEP("pre: mux-apple-display-crossbar macsmc-power");
+MODULE_SOFTDEP("pre: mux-apple-display-crossbar atc-t6050-dp macsmc-power");
